create the stirrups
  aka stirrup display, stirrups display, ordinary stirrups, riding stirrups
  scenery, a supporter, plural
  stall-display
  in the Leather Stall

  They're ordinary riding stirrups, for getting up on horses.

create the scabbards
  aka scabbard display, scabbards display, sheaths, plain scabbards, unadorned scabbards
  scenery, a supporter, plural
  stall-display
  in the Leather Stall

  The scabbards are mostly plain, unadorned leather, good for sliding a sword
  into and not much else.

create the rack of belts
  aka rack, belt rack, belts, belts display, sturdy belts, well-crafted belts
  scenery, a supporter
  stall-display
  in the Leather Stall

  The belts on display here aren't anything fancy, but they're sturdy and
  well-crafted.

create the riding reins
  aka reins, rein, useless reins
  leather-ware-plural
  plural
  states: shelved, nicked
  on the collective reins

  They're ordinary riding reins, used for steering horses. What use they are
  to you without a horse, you're not sure yet.

create the harness
  aka leather harness, tough harness, complicated contraption, contraption
  leather-ware
  states: shelved, nicked
  on the harnesses

  It's a complicated contraption of tough leather straps and buckles, for
  hitching horses to wagons.

create the stirrup
  aka riding stirrup, ordinary stirrup
  leather-ware
  states: shelved, nicked
  on the stirrups

  It's an ordinary riding stirrup, for getting up on a horse. What use it is
  to you without a horse, you're not sure yet.

create the plain scabbard
  aka scabbard, sheath, unadorned scabbard, leather scabbard, good scabbard
  wearable
  leather-ware
  states: shelved, nicked
  on the scabbards

  It's a sheath of plain, unadorned leather. You've got no sword to put in
  it, nor any belt to hang it on, but for all that it's a perfectly good
  scabbard.

  on the player wearing
    refuse scabbard-needs-belt
  end on

create the belt
  aka good belt, sturdy belt, leather belt, strap, well-crafted belt
  wearable
  leather-ware
  states: shelved, nicked
  on the rack of belts

  Now, a good belt is always useful. This one isn't anything fancy, but it's
  sturdy and well-crafted.

define phrase leather-smell
  The smell of leather always makes you think of traveling in distant,
  dangerous lands. It's the smell of camping out under the stars, the smell
  of adventure.
end phrase

define phrase saddle-too-huge
  The saddle is way too huge for you to nick. Anyway, horses make you
  nervous.
end phrase

define phrase scabbard-needs-belt
  You need a belt in order to wear this thing.
end phrase

