## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
## THE EXOTIC GEMS STALL (`story.ni:2649-2690`) — nothing here can be nicked
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

create the precious gems
  aka gems, gem, jewels, cheap gems, smuggled gems, display, displays, fare, wares, merchandise, goods
  scenery, plural
  in the Exotic Gems Stall

  Some of them are loose stones; others are set in finely wrought rings and
  necklaces. Most of them were probably illegally smuggled from over the
  western mountains, which is why they're cheap enough to be affordable by
  anyone in Grubber's Market. Still, they're far, far out of your price
  range.

  on the player taking
    refuse gems-glaring
  end on

create the loose stones
  aka stones, stone, gemstones, gemstone, gem stones, loose gems, tiny stones, shiny stones
  scenery, plural
  in the Exotic Gems Stall

  Most of the loose stones are tiny, some no bigger than your little
  fingernail. They sure are shiny, though.

  on the player taking
    refuse gems-glaring
  end on

create the pretty jewelry
  aka jewelry, jewelery, rings, ring, necklaces, flashy jewelry, flashy rings
  scenery, plural
  in the Exotic Gems Stall

  The rings and necklaces are pretty, but they all look a bit *too* flashy.
  You have a sneaking suspicion that some of them might turn your skin green
  if you wore them too long.

  on the player taking
    refuse gems-glaring
  end on

define phrase gems-glaring
  The angry stallkeeper is constantly glaring at you; there's no way you'd
  manage to nick something and get away with it.
end phrase

